    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate with **Junior Caminero** (78.72) and **Yordan Alvarez** (75.77) headlining our offensive attack. **Junior Caminero** earns the top spot in the utility slot due to a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (4.74 xERA), while **Yordan Alvarez** remains an auto-start with his elite .452 xwOBA, proving his value even against a neutral arm in Kolek. Our focus on speed continues to pay dividends in the outfield, where **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (62.50) projects as an elite play. His aggressive position in the leadoff spot combined with a significant platoon advantage against Logan Webb elevates his scoring potential well above his base projection.\n\nPlatoon edges are driving our strategy for the remaining outfield spots, where **Carson Benge** (58.64) and **Lars Nootbaar** (58.58) provide strong efficiency ratings. **Lars Nootbaar** is particularly intriguing today; while facing Tyler Bradley (4.18 xERA), his +11% dynamic platoon boost and strong .388 xwOBA make him a vital asset for maintaining our batting average and RBI output. Conversely, **Gary Sanchez** (43.23) remains a marginal play at catcher; he is weighed down significantly by a tough matchup against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez (2.72 xERA), whose elite pitching skill acts as a major drag on **Gary Sanchez**'s overall scoring potential.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just outside the starting lineup with a 38.81 rating. Despite a favorable wind condition, the high xERA of opposing pitcher Bryan Sheehan (3.38) pushed **Chase Meidroth** below our strict 40.0 efficiency floor, forcing us to prioritize the higher-upside profiles of our active infielders. With **Hyeseong Kim**, **Rece Hinds**, and **Colt Keith** currently unavailable due to minor league assignments or a confirmed rainout, we have limited flexibility on the bench. We will continue to monitor the lineups for **Kyle Schwarber**, whose leadoff duties against Harrison (3.39 xERA) remain a point of interest; while his score of 56.05 is solid, the matchup against a sub-3.50 xERA arm mandates a watchful eye for any late defensive substitutions that could curtail his plate appearances.",
